    </section>

    <section class="section-padding am-info-section">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="row g-4 mb-5">
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="am-info-tile text-center p-4 h-100">
                        <span class="am-highlight-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-handshake"></i></span>
                        <h4 class="mt-3">Mutual Trust</h4>
                        <p class="mb-0">Clear and respectful guidelines designed to support parents, students, and tutors.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="am-info-tile text-center p-4 h-100">
                        <span class="am-highlight-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-calendar-check"></i></span>
                        <h4 class="mt-3">Flexible Attendance</h4>
                        <p class="mb-0">Fair scheduling and advance rescheduling policies to support busy modern families.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="col-md-4">
                    <div class="am-info-tile text-center p-4 h-100">
                        <span class="am-highlight-icon"><i class="fa-solid fa-lock"></i></span>
                        <h4 class="mt-3">Data Integrity</h4>
                        <p class="mb-0">Full adherence to student privacy and protected educational materials.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <article class="am-info-card wow fadeInUp">
                <div class="section-heading text-center mb-40">
                    <span>Academy Agreement</span>
                    <h2>Terms of Service &amp; Policies</h2>
                    <img src="assets/img/icons/title.ico" alt="" />
                </div>

                <div class="am-legal-block mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h5 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-2"></i>1. Introduction</h3>
                    <p>Welcome to Al-Asim Quran. By accessing our website, enrolling in our online courses, or participating in trial sessions, you agree to comply with and be bound by the following Terms &amp; Conditions. Please read them carefully before using our services.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="am-legal-block mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h5 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-2"></i>2. Enrollment Policy</h3>
                    <p>Students or their legal guardians must provide accurate, current, and complete information during the registration process. Al-Asim Quran reserves the right to accept or decline any enrollment application at its discretion to maintain quality and security across all batches.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="am-legal-block mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h5 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-2"></i>3. Class Attendance &amp; Punctuality</h3>
                    <p>Students are expected to attend all scheduled classes regularly and join on time. Consistent attendance is essential for Quranic memorization, Tajweed fluency, and academic progress. Teachers wait in the virtual classroom for up to 15 minutes past the start time.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="am-legal-block mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h5 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-2"></i>4. Scheduling &amp; Rescheduling</h3>
                    <p>Class schedules are arranged based on mutual availability between the student and the academy. If a student needs to reschedule a class, they must notify the administration at least 6 hours in advance. Make-up classes will be scheduled subject to teacher availability.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="am-legal-block mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h5 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-2"></i>5. Fee Policy &amp; Monthly Dues</h3>
                    <p>Course fees are billed in advance on a monthly basis according to the agreed plan (Basic, Standard, or Premium). Timely payment ensures continuous scheduling and teacher allocation. Classes may be temporarily paused if dues remain unpaid past the due date.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="am-legal-block mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h5 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-2"></i>6. Free Trial Class</h3>
                    <p>Free trial classes are offered to new students for evaluation of our teaching methodology, tutor interaction, and learning platform. Participation in a trial session carries no financial obligation and does not automatically commit the student to full enrollment.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="am-legal-block mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h5 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-2"></i>7. Student &amp; Guardian Conduct</h3>
                    <p>Al-Asim Quran maintains a respectful, Islamic, and welcoming atmosphere. Disrespectful behavior, harassment, inappropriate language, or unauthorized recording of class sessions is strictly prohibited and grounds for immediate termination without refund.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="am-legal-block mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h5 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-2"></i>8. Teacher Assignment &amp; Preferences</h3>
                    <p>Both male and female teachers are available. While we make every effort to accommodate teacher preferences and maintain consistent tutor assignments, Al-Asim Quran reserves the right to reassign instructors when necessary due to health, leave, or operational requirements.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="am-legal-block mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h5 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-2"></i>9. Intellectual Property</h3>
                    <p>All syllabus outlines, Noorani Qaida notes, Tajweed audio-visual charts, lesson slides, and brand assets remain the exclusive intellectual property of Al-Asim Quran. Course materials are provided strictly for individual personal study and may not be commercially redistributed.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="am-legal-block mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h5 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-2"></i>10. Limitation of Liability</h3>
                    <p>Al-Asim Quran strives to deliver uninterrupted online lessons, but is not liable for interruptions resulting from third-party internet service disruptions, software outages (Zoom, Google Meet, Skype), power failures, or unforeseen circumstances beyond our reasonable control.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="am-legal-block mb-4">
                    <h3 class="h5 text-dark fw-bold"><i class="fa-solid fa-circle-check text-success me-2"></i>11. Policy Modifications</h3>
                    <p>Al-Asim Quran reserves the right to update or modify these Terms &amp; Conditions periodically. Any updates will be published on this page with an updated revision date. Continued participation in our classes constitutes acceptance of updated terms.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="p-4 bg-light rounded text-muted">
                    <p class="mb-1"><strong>Last Updated:</strong> June 2026</p>
                    <p class="mb-0">Questions regarding these terms? Contact our administration at <a href="mailto:alasimquran@gmail.com">alasimquran@gmail.com</a> or visit our <a href="inquiry.aspx">Inquiry Page</a>.</p>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>
    </section>
</asp:Content>
